- ### Elements that are not numbers
+ ### Elementos que no son números

- Nothing above requires the entries to be `Double`s. Vectors and matrices are generic in their
- element type, and their operations are found through the arithmetic typeclasses, so anything
- with the right structure works. That includes typed [quantities](quantities.md), whose
- dimensions compose as the arithmetic does:
+ Nada de lo anterior exige que las entradas sean `Double`s. Los vectores y las matrices son
+ genéricos en el tipo de sus elementos, y sus operaciones se encuentran mediante las clases de
+ tipos aritméticas, así que funciona cualquier cosa con la estructura adecuada. Eso incluye las
+ [magnitudes](quantities.md) con tipo, cuyas dimensiones se combinan igual que la aritmética:

= dimensions compose as the arithmetic does:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val v1 = Vector(5*Inch, 2*Inch, Inch)
+ val v1 = Vector(5*Inch, 2*Inch, Inch)

- val v2 = Vector(2*Inch, 3*Inch, 6*Inch)
+ val v2 = Vector(2*Inch, 3*Inch, 6*Inch)

= val v2 = Vector(2*Inch, 3*Inch, 6*Inch)
- ```
+ ```

= val v2 = Vector(2*Inch, 3*Inch, 6*Inch)
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val v2 = Vector(2*Inch, 3*Inch, 6*Inch)
= ```
