- Internally, a permutation is stored as its
- [Lehmer code](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lehmer_code) in factorial-base form, which is a
- single integer that uniquely identifies it. That makes permutations compact to store and to
- enumerate: `Permutation.bySize(n)` gives all `n!` of them, as a lazy
- [chain](collections.md#lazy-chains). A permutation of *n* elements occupies
- O(*n* log *n*) space, which is the least possible, since there are *n*! of them to tell apart.
+ Internamente, una permutación se almacena como su
+ [código de Lehmer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lehmer_code) en base factorial, que es un único
+ entero que la identifica de forma unívoca. Eso hace que las permutaciones sean compactas de
+ almacenar y de enumerar: `Permutation.bySize(n)` da las `n!`, como una
+ [cadena](collections.md#lazy-chains) perezosa. Una permutación de *n* elementos ocupa un espacio
+ O(*n* log *n*), que es el mínimo posible, ya que hay *n*! que distinguir.

- The number *is* the permutation, so it can be given directly, and both representations can be
- read back:
+ El número *es* la permutación, así que se puede dar directamente, y ambas representaciones se
+ pueden volver a leer:

= read back:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= read back:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= read back:
